config ENTROPY_RP2040_ROSC
	bool "RP2040 ring-oscillator entropy driver"
	default y
	depends on SOC_SERIES_RP2040
	depends on SYS_CLOCK_EXISTS
	depends on DT_HAS_RASPBERRYPI_RP2040_ROSC_RNG_ENABLED
	select ENTROPY_HAS_DRIVER
	select ENTROPY_NEEDS_PRNG
	help
	  Read the RP2040 ring oscillator's random-bit register directly, without
	  the Pico SDK random generator. RP2040 has no hardware TRNG, so this is
	  the platform entropy source, as in the Pico SDK's pico_rand and
	  pico_mbedtls. The RP2040 datasheet does not recommend the ring
	  oscillator for security applications; use an external TRNG or secure
	  element where stronger guarantees are required.
	  The oscillator must be enabled and stable, and the system clock must
	  use XOSC or a PLL. Clock configuration must remain unchanged during
	  a request. This driver does not reconfigure or enable the oscillator.
